<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlisle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Luguvalium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlisle is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumbria">Cumbria</a>, north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, near the Scottish border, on the site of the Roman town of Luguvalium close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadrians-wall">Hadrian's Wall</a>. It was the centre of the civitas of the Carvetii and later a stronghold disputed between England and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, with a castle and a cathedral founded in the 12th century. It is the main town of Cumbria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlisle.jpg" alt="Carlisle" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bill Harrison · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlisle_Market_Cross_6310907_2233337d.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
